A||||16||frontal lobe||road trip||||1||
Z||000000||frontal lobe||08-31-2000||10:58 PM||||My wife and I leave on a plane Friday from Milwaukee to Naples, Florida.  I found a '95 Mazda Miata with 62000 miles on it for only $6300 via the internet.  Too far for me to go check it out because it was just north of Miami.  Fortunately for me, my brother-in-law lives in Naples so he was able to go over and check it out for me.  More fortune--he's a mechanic at the Naples Cadillac dealership so he was able to check out the car and it was solid.  So I wired the money to his bank and he went and bought it for me about 6 weeks ago.  This weekend we finally get a chance to fly down and then drive it back.  Hope the weather is good so I can get some top-down driving in.  My wife has always wanted one of these and this one was so reasonable I couldn't pass it up.<P>Question:  Is the small gas tank likely to empty before the average female bladder fills?  Trying to guess the number of stops over the 1400 mile trip home.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-01-2000||12:15 AM||||My wife used to ride with me when I drove a truck.  I'm guessing about 70 stops in a 1400 mile trip. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||09-01-2000||12:30 AM||||Congrats on the new purchase! I remember back in 93/94 I was dating this 17 year old VERY wealthy girl who had a red conv. Miata..man it was nice! I really like those cars. I like the older ones better though (the ones with the pop up headlights).<P>By the way, Im only a couple of years older than her, dont go thinking Im so perverted old man!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||frontal lobe||09-01-2000||01:03 AM||||Monkeyman, no wonder you got off the road.  With her along, you could hardly get ON the road!  NO FLUIDS for my wife on this trip.<P>My7Fieros, I didn't think you were a pervert.  With you being from the south, and she being 17, I assumed she was an old maid still being single at that age, and that you were probably like 13 or 14!  Just kidding.  That's a northerner's stereotype of the south.  We all know that it's KENTUCKY where that happens!  (again, just teasing.  Please to my forum friends in Kentucky, just joking).  I didn't even assume you were related!<P>The '95 model still has the pop-up headlights.  In '94 they went to a 1.8 liter engine instead of the 1.6, so a FEW more horsepower.  It should be fun.  My wife will be the majority driver.  It's more up her alley.  I'll stick to the 5-speed v6 Fiero GT.  It's a little "crude" (vs refined) for her (it doesn't have power steering) but perfect for me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||09-01-2000||09:14 AM||||Good purchase!<BR>My wife used to have a '90 Miata. Sold it last summer. (She got nervous, seeing the 18-wheelers towering over her on I-20.) She still misses that car. Only thing I didn't like about it was the automatic trans. <BR>When Mazda designed the Miata, they were attempting to copy the feel of an MG. IMHO, they hit the nail on the head. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||09-01-2000||11:13 PM||||Ahhhh!! Making fun of the south are ya? Well, maybe its because you're just too full from beer and cheese...while watching Happy Days and Lavern and Shirley!! Isnt that what everybody in Wisconsin does?<P>JUST KIDDING!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Post some pics of the Miata soon! And again, congrats on the purchase!||||reg||6
Z||000006||wkayl||09-02-2000||10:07 AM||||My wife's sister's son has a friend that has a red "Monster Miata" conv.  It has some sort of V-8 in it.  He has many tickets from showing off with it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||09-02-2000||07:50 PM||||Yeah. That's one of the more insane swaps that I've heard about. &lt;Insert Tim Allen grunting noises, here.&gt;<P>Check this link... <A HREF="http://www.monstermotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.monstermotorsports.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000008||frontal lobe||09-04-2000||01:27 AM||||My7Fieros, good one!  You nailed me!  Laverne and Shirley is EXACTLY like Milwaukee--only 40 years ago.  No beer for me, but the cheese is right on...and don't forget the bratwurst.<P>Made it back fine with the car.  Bonus:  turns out it has a leather interior!  Black with tan interior and tan top.  Has the 5-speed transmission (otherwise, what's the point--right, Raydar?!?)<P>I was cranking on it--80 to 85mph sustained.  Ran like a champ.  30mpg at those speeds.  My wife is thrilled with it.  I like it, too.  Could use a little more horsepower for my taste, but it sure handles well.  No plans to do a v8 conversion!||||reg||1
Z||000009||hugh||09-04-2000||09:56 AM||||How many stops on the way back?or did you wear depens.You should have used your stop in Florida to further your singing career.||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||09-04-2000||10:16 AM||||Got the perfect swap for you... buy my Mazda 323 GTX. Has the same 1.6 dohc that was in the early Miatas, then turbocharged and intercooled for fun! Be the first kid on your block with a turbo Miata! Will sell for cheap! Make Offer!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||09-04-2000||09:43 PM||||Just told my wife about the Miata that you bought. When I told her what it was, and how much, she said "Wow!"<BR>When I told her it had leather upholstery, she said "Ooooooooh!"<BR>(Like I said, she really misses that car.)<BR>Congrats again, on your find! I hope it proves to be everything that ours was.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000012||frontal lobe||09-04-2000||10:39 PM||||Hugh, forget the Depends.  No matter how absorbant they are, I still get that annoying diaper rash.  Fortunately, being in the medical field, we could wear indwelling (foley) catheters and leg bags!  Just kidding.  Drove through Nashville and thought of furthering the singing career there, but seems like Willie Nelson has the "elderly" singer market sewed up.<P>Raydar, my wife is still smiling.  Hope we have a decent end of summer, and fall.  Labor day--cold wind out of the north and high of 68 degrees.  Not ideal top-down weather.  Stupid Wisconsin summers.<P>Stimpy, you are not going to believe this but I have always wanted a 323GT turbo!  I have always liked Mazdas and have had good luck with them.  I had an '88 626 turbo 4-door.  No special badges so everyone thought it was just another ho-hum, generic Japanese sedan.  It had the 2.2 that Ford shared with the Probe GT.  I don't know how they got away with rating it at 145 hp and yet it was rated at 190 torque!  I had the 5-speed so it really hauled once the turbo got spooled up.  Only bad thing was with the front-wheel drive and that much power, the front end would unload and it would torque steer like mad.  That's ok.  It was kind of fun to just grab the steering wheel, floor it, and hang on and see what direction it was going to go!  Oh yeah, it was intercooled, too.  I finally got rid of it after 8 years and got a Millenia S with the supercharged, intercooled engine.  Badly needs a 5-speed but not available.  Bummer.  I bet the GTX is fun.  Is that 4 wheel drive?  Can't do a swap, though.  My wife says hands-off the Miata.  No swaps, bolt-ons, enhancements, anything.  She likes it the way it is.  Oh well, all my supercharger research for nought.<P>One comment I have to make about the drive home.  Good thing it's a convertible so lots of wind noise, because the way they have it geared, 4000 rpm at 80mph!!!!!  4000 rpm!  4200 at 85mph.  Man.  At least the engine wasn't buzzy, but still.  Would it have cost that much to put a 6th overdrive gear in??? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||09-04-2000||11:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, lucidatypewriter">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B> <BR>Stimpy, you are not going to believe this but I have always wanted a 323GT turbo!  I bet the GTX is fun.  Is that 4 wheel drive? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep, it's full time all wheel drive with electronic differentail lock. It still has less then 100k miles and runs super quiet at idle, but rev her up to that 6500 redline and it's screaming like a banshee. I'm tellin ya doc, you need this car! It would take to Wisconsin winters like a pig to sh... well, you know. It is kinda rough looking, was actually a salvage title in CA, so as a restoration project, it's a bust.  But it drives straight, has much better brakes then my Fiero, and sad to say, is a little quicker too. Something like 145 hp and 153 lbs torque with zero wheelspin. Can't even spin the tires in soapy snow! But you can drive it sideways...hehehe.  Well, if you know anyone who might be interested in making a rally car or just have a fun winter beater, I could definately use the extra cash to help pay for my upcoming wedding. Let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000014||frontal lobe||09-05-2000||02:05 PM||||Stimpy, you are killing me!  You know I want the car.  I wanted it quite a while ago when in a previous thread you mentioned you needed to sell it.  But my wife would KILL me if I brought home another car.  I've been bringing them home lately like stray cats.  I'm up to five now.  As it is now, I need to sell one of the Fiero's.<P>Hey Raydar, I forgot to mention I drove through your neck of the woods on the way home.  Ate at a Carraba's just off I-75 in Smyrna?  Then stayed overnight in Ringgold.  Did we come close to you?||||reg||1
Z||000015||stimpy||09-05-2000||07:58 PM||||Easy answer, got a spare automatic trans Fiero lying around? Simple trade. hehe. Really though if we ask her real nice will she let you get it?<P>New stuff on it includes struts, brakes, recent Pirelli tires, new interstate battery.  Interior is in good condition, no cracks in dash, no tears or burns in seat, transaxle/differential works fine, digital dash works. Excellent donor car to redo a tired GTX, or a great winter beater.  Someone buy my car! ||||reg||1
Z||000016||frontal lobe||09-06-2000||11:56 PM||||Sorry, Stimpy.  No possible way.  She wouldn't mind me spending the money, but no where to put it.  Regarding the Fiero's, I'm a manual man so both mine are not automatics.  Sorry.||||reg||1
